<title>USA: Adolph Coors says board oks $40 million.</title>
<headline>Adolph Coors says board oks $40 million.</headline>
<dateline>GOLDEN, Colo. 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Adolph Coors Co said its board has authorized the expenditure of up to $40 million to repurchase its outstanding Class B common stock from time to time during 1997.</p>
<p>Any repurchases, which are expected to begin in early 1997, may be made through the open market or in privately negotiated transactions and will be financed through funds generated from operations or borrowed on established lines of credit.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610</p>
</text>
